# Repository Standards & Git Workflow

## Branching & Release Model
- Default Branch: `develop`
- Production Branch: `main`
- Workflow: Feature branches (`feature/<description>`) -> Merge to `develop` (`--no-ff`) -> Periodic release merge to `main`.
- Issue Tracking: Link commits/branches to GitHub issues using `gh` CLI commands.

## Privacy & Hygiene Rules
- NEVER include local file paths (e.g., `/Users/...`, `/home/...`, `C:\...`), user names, or machine identifiers in code, docstrings, commit messages, or markdown documentation.
- Maintain a strict `.gitignore` to exclude bytecode, `.venv`, `.DS_Store`, build artifacts, and egg-info files.

## Documentation & Testing Standards
- Provide complete code, comprehensive unit tests (`pytest`), and clear CLI execution commands.
- Maintain updated math and architecture documentation in `docs/` alongside code changes.
